   116	/// Writes `plan` to disk and stages the touched paths in git.
   117	///
   118	/// Every side effect here is unconditional -- whether to apply at all is
   119	/// the caller's decision, which is why an [`ApplyPermit`] is required
   120	/// rather than a `dry_run` bool: a bool carries no guarantee any caller
   121	/// actually consulted it. A dry-run caller can't obtain a permit and
   122	/// simply doesn't call this function; it reports `plan` instead.
   123	///
   124	/// # Errors
   125	///
   126	/// - Manifest parse/write failures (malformed TOML/JSON, unsupported format).
   127	/// - Git subprocess failures (`git add`/`git rm --cached` non-zero exit).
   128	/// - I/O errors writing changelog sections or `pre.json`.
